LRC tournament-computation speedup roadmap (S583)
Scores: certificate_safety, proof_payoff, algorithmic_leverage, -cost, maturity.

Priority order
 1. Cprime_gate_tournament_calculus      priority=37 key=(5, 5, 5, -3, 5) source=THM-398, HYP-2105/2108/2112, lrc_n14_certificate_calculus_s580.py, lrc_circuit_to_gap_functional_s576.py
    preserves: proof obligations, residual gates, Phi/P gap functionals, and named exits
    destroys:  fine speed realization labels unless endpoint owners are carried
    next:      Compile gates into a decision DAG whose terminal middle circuits call Phi(C)/P(S).
 2. observer_source_marked_reachability  priority=36 key=(5, 5, 4, -2, 5) source=THM-381, lrc_observer_source_tournament_s511.py
    preserves: exact LRC predicate: observer lonely iff marked observer is a source
    destroys:  continuous time geometry after cell/class projection
    next:      Build a marked-class transition automaton with source targets precomputed.
 3. goodcut_SCC_protection_core          priority=31 key=(4, 4, 4, -2, 5) source=THM-354, THM-395, good-cut-count.md, tournament_tda.py
    preserves: endpoint-protection core shape via SCC defect and backward-wedge debt
    destroys:  arithmetic labels on protector intervals unless attached separately
    next:      Attach SCC/private-leaf peeling to endpoint-owner and pressure graphs.
 4. threshold_decorated_quotient_stack   priority=29 key=(4, 4, 4, -3, 4) source=lrc_restricted_tournament_mappings_s535.py, lrc_section_boundary_functors_s539.py
    preserves: good-only class fibers after observer/source/gap/threshold labels
    destroys:  purity if labels are dropped; raw phase classes mix good and bad
    next:      Use good-only colored fibers as fast certificate targets before exact search.
 5. three_state_middle_automata          priority=27 key=(3, 5, 4, -3, 3) source=HYP-2109, tournament_three_state_automaton_s582.py
    preserves: left/right owner exits and middle wall survival before projection
    destroys:  metric margin unless M cells keep length/residue labels
    next:      Make endpoint-owner and residue cells emit L/M/R event words.
 6. Burnside_restricted_orbit_counts     priority=27 key=(3, 4, 5, -4, 4) source=HYP-2097, HYP-2099, A000568/Burnside quotient scripts
    preserves: symmetry quotient counts and orbit representatives
    destroys:  endpoint/pair certificates until labels are reattached
    next:      Refine A000568(13)->round316->merged190->fixed64 with owner labels.
 7. A2_iso_fingerprint_lookup            priority=27 key=(3, 3, 5, -2, 4) source=fractal-isomorphism-via-a2.md, a2_applications_s339.py
    preserves: tournament isomorphism class through n<=9; strong hash beyond
    destroys:  proof certainty beyond verified range unless backed by canonical fallback
    next:      Use sorted A^2 rows as first-pass cache key for LRC quotient walks.
 8. cheap_TDA_prefilter                  priority=24 key=(2, 3, 4, -1, 5) source=tournament_tda.py, tournament_tda_residue_features_s355.out
    preserves: score, c3, SCC defect, residue rank, Omega packet summaries
    destroys:  the LRC threshold predicate; cannot certify alone
    next:      Emit LRC JSON fingerprints for each quotient cell and rank residuals.
 9. near_transitive_perturbation_DP      priority=22 key=(2, 3, 5, -3, 3) source=applications-probe-2026-05-30.md, algorithmic_breakthroughs_s90ai.out
    preserves: small upset set relative to a base order or tie-wall perturbation
    destroys:  global class exactness when the upset set is not small
    next:      Parameterize AP/Vstar/tie-wall neighborhoods by upset set k and update locally.

